  "prompt": "Build Datamosh from the v4 200×150px photo-trails frame at (86,28) in its 372×264 stage, with 14px corners and the unchanged supplied border SVG. Match the exact cover crop and five initial 30×20px fragments at (40,40), (80,40), (60,80), (100,80), (120,60), each at .85 opacity with the original +10px horizontal source offset. Active native corruption projects the complete original twelve-block, three-trail feedback buffer through these five fixed crop windows at compact resolution; full retains its 368×268 field and uses photo-ocean. Preserve the 8px grid, seven focus-biased blocks, seeded scratch snapshots, 70ms corruption threshold, 1050ms burst and automatic recovery. Expose Corrupt frame and Restore frame; physical hover and arrows move the original focus. Credit Osman Rana and Michael Benz. Keep a 240×168 hero plane and a separate complete 400×400 full view with native scrolling and readable Geist/Geist Mono. Prefix classes with rootClass; place actions in the shell. Preserve every original source state, dataset, duration, seeded random sequence, automatic cadence and interruption. Normalize pointer and touch coordinates through the actual fitted field; retain arrow keys, Home, Space/Enter and Escape, independent caller/viewport pauses, ordered queued intent and complete cleanup. Reduced motion uses a deliberate still and interruptible 150ms opacity feedback. Embed local approved photos, fonts and licence comments in network-independent exports.",
